{"id":"u-212c6bc9-af31-4a98-a928-95dbe2b229cb","src":"community","title":"Phase 3 -  Specificity and Taper (Sprinters)","author":"Dylan Garner","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/YC3K66-phase-2-speed-and-power-sprinters-pushpull","desc":"To build the Specificity and to Taper down for your 100 meter test. For sprinting and overall body strength. Perform every non sprint/leg related lift TILL FAILURE. Leave no reps in reserve when it comes to the non sprint/leg related lifts.  Based on a research article and is a plan I follow myself. This plan lasts 4 weeks and has 3 total phases. each phase lasts 4 weeks.\n\nREST TIMES:\nTraditional: 65-75% 1RM - 1-2 Minutes — 85% 1RM - 3-5 Minutes\nWeightlifting: 3-5 Minutes\nPlyometric: Short - 2-3 Minutes — Long - 3-5 Minutes\nMaximum Velocity Runs (40-80m): 5-10 Minutes\nSprint Endurance (80-150m): 8-15 Minutes\nLactate Tolerance Work: (Planned Incomplete Recovery) 2-3 Minutes\n\nCheck out the video I made on the entirety of sprint research: \nhttps://youtu.be/sHRYI9GU-6M?si=R4I_AYTvcrl3F0ZC\n\nResearch Article I based this on:\nWU, YAO. “Integrating Strength, Speed, and Endurance: A Comprehensive Training Model for 100M and 400M Sprints.” Retos, vol. 67, JURUFRA SL, May 2025, pp. 1200–10, https://doi.org/10.47197/retos.v67.114886. Accessed 28 Aug. 2026.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Bodyweight Fitness","Strength","Athletics"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":60,"joins":4,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-02T15:22:24.292Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Track","Push/Pull/Legs","Rest","Track","Track","Light Push/Pull Workout","Rest"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Track","sets":[{}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Cossack Squat","sets":[{"lo":9,"hi":11,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Plank (Weighted)","sets":[{"sec":20,"secHi":30,"pct":75}]},{"n":"Military Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":1